---
title: "Phase 1 architecture, part 1 of 2 — ingestion"
---
classDiagram
    direction TB

    class IngestionPipeline {
        <<Template Method>>
        +run()
        -_fetch()
        -_adapt()
        -_normalize()
        -_validate()
        -_dedup()
        -_append()
    }
    note for IngestionPipeline "TEMPLATE METHOD - the step ORDER is fixed, every step is injected"

    class SourceAdapter {
        <<abstract>>
        +source_id
        +fetch()
        +adapt()
    }
    class PangaeaAdapter
    class BoxcoreSummaryAdapter
    class NoduleAggregateAdapter
    class TabularFileAdapter
    class RegionalGridAdapter
    note for SourceAdapter "ADAPTER - one class per source FAMILY, not per source"

    SourceAdapter <|-- PangaeaAdapter
    SourceAdapter <|-- TabularFileAdapter
    SourceAdapter <|-- RegionalGridAdapter
    SourceAdapter <|-- NoduleAggregateAdapter
    PangaeaAdapter <|-- BoxcoreSummaryAdapter

    class AbundanceNormalizer {
        <<abstract>>
        +normalize(record)
    }
    class MassNormalizer
    class CountNormalizer
    class CoverNormalizer
    class GridNormalizer
    class GradeNormalizer
    note for AbundanceNormalizer "STRATEGY - one interchangeable rule per evidence class"
    note for CoverNormalizer "the hard rule lives here - never sets abundance_kg_m2"

    AbundanceNormalizer <|-- MassNormalizer
    AbundanceNormalizer <|-- CountNormalizer
    AbundanceNormalizer <|-- CoverNormalizer
    AbundanceNormalizer <|-- GridNormalizer
    AbundanceNormalizer <|-- GradeNormalizer

    class NormalizerRegistry {
        <<Registry>>
        +register(evidence_class, normalizer)
        +normalize(record)
        +assert_complete()
    }
    note for NormalizerRegistry "REGISTRY - selection is data-driven, and assert_complete makes a forgotten class fail loudly"

    NormalizerRegistry o-- AbundanceNormalizer

    class DuplicateResolutionPolicy {
        <<policy, pure>>
        +resolve(candidate) Resolution
    }
    note for DuplicateResolutionPolicy "PURE - it decides and returns; the pipeline applies. Replaced a Specification that decided and mutated in one call"

    class Resolution {
        <<sealed base>>
    }
    class Admit {
        +candidate
    }
    class AlreadyPresent {
        +candidate
        +existing
    }
    class AbsorbInto {
        +merged
        +donated_fields
        +note
        +escalated_status
    }
    class Replace {
        +merged
        +donated_fields
        +note
        +escalated_status
    }
    note for Resolution "VALUE OBJECT - names what should happen, so nothing is hidden behind a bool"

    Resolution <|-- Admit
    Resolution <|-- AlreadyPresent
    Resolution <|-- AbsorbInto
    Resolution <|-- Replace

    class Observation {
        <<domain type>>
        +evidence_class
        +abundance_kg_m2
        +qa_status
        +is_training_eligible()
    }
    note for Observation "enforces the evidence-class rules at construction - a COVER row with a mass value cannot be built"

    IngestionPipeline --> SourceAdapter : fetch and adapt
    IngestionPipeline --> NormalizerRegistry : normalize
    IngestionPipeline --> Observation : validate
    IngestionPipeline --> DuplicateResolutionPolicy : resolve
    DuplicateResolutionPolicy ..> Resolution : returns
    IngestionPipeline ..> Resolution : applies

%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
%% CAPTION
%%
%% What this shows: the ingestion half of the engine, with the design pattern
%% each cluster implements. Audience is a reviewer, not Isaac.
%%
%% Read it as four seams. ADAPTER absorbs the fact that every published source
%% has its own file format, so the pipeline never learns what a PANGAEA tab
%% file looks like. STRATEGY puts each evidence class's scientific rule in its
%% own small class -- which is why the COVER rule can be tested in isolation
%% and verified by deliberately breaking it. REGISTRY makes "did we forget an
%% evidence class" a test that fails rather than a silent gap. TEMPLATE METHOD
%% fixes the step order while letting every step be swapped.
%%
%% The DuplicateResolutionPolicy is the one place a pattern was RETIRED. It
%% used to implement a Specification with an is_satisfied_by method that
%% returned a boolean while quietly rewriting the corpus -- and that mismatch
%% between the advertised contract and the real one caused a live bug. It now
%% returns a Resolution value object naming exactly what should happen, and
%% the pipeline is the only thing that writes.
%%
